Review one member form of a multilingual wordnet used to teach vocabulary.

Wordnets list, for each concept, the words ("member forms") that express it in a
language. Some entries are not words at all: a definition pasted in as if it were a
word, text in the wrong language, or a garbled or duplicated string. Long multiword
names and terms are normal and must be kept ("Academie militaire de West Point",
"transistor a effet de champ", a person's full name, a species name).

Language: {{ language }}
Member form: {{ form }}
English gloss of the concept: {{ english_definition }}
English member forms of the concept: {{ english_members }}
Other {{ language }} member forms of the concept: {{ other_forms }}

Decide:
- `kind`: one of "term" (a word, compound or multiword term), "name" (a proper
  name), "definition" (it explains the meaning instead of naming it), "wrong
  language" (not {{ language }}), or "garbled" (broken, duplicated, or markup).
- `drop`: true only for "definition", "wrong language" or "garbled".
- `reason`: one short English sentence.
